1.bug_scenario:
In v11 of @carbon/react, destructuring sub-components (TableContainer, Table, TableHead, TableRow, TableHeader, TableBody, TableCell) directly off the default DataTable export yields undefined and breaks the app (React.createElement: type is invalid). For example:

  import { DataTable } from '@carbon/react';
  const { TableContainer, Table, TableHead, TableRow, TableHeader, TableBody, TableCell } = DataTable;

causes console errors and no rendering. Switching to direct named imports:

  import { DataTable, TableContainer, Table, TableHead, TableRow, TableHeader, TableBody, TableCell } from '@carbon/react';

resolves the issue, indicating that DataTable does not currently expose its sub-components as static properties on its default export.
